      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg per day. A dose that high could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and shock. It could also cause non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema, and those effects can last a long time because the drug's half-life is long.\n\nYou also mentioned that you aren't a clinician. Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber who is responsible for the patient.\n\n- **If 50 mg was a typo,** I can enter the standard dose. The usual adult dose is 5 mg by mouth once daily, and it can be increased to 10 mg. Please confirm the intended dose.\n- **If the prescriber really intends 50 mg,** they should confirm it directly. They can also work with pharmacy to enter it with a documented rationale.\n\nTell me the corrected dose, or have the prescriber contact me, and I'll enter the order."
      }
