       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change my answer. The dose is still five times the maximum, and you've told me you aren't the prescriber. Neither fact has changed. Entering it could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere are options that would let this move forward safely:\n\n- **If a typo is the cause,** I can enter amlodipine 5 mg by mouth once daily right now. I can also enter 10 mg, which is the maximum. Just tell me which one.\n- **If the treating prescriber wants a nonstandard dose,** they should enter or confirm it themselves and consult pharmacy. They would need to document the clinical rationale. I can help with that once they are involved.\n- **If you are worried about this patient's blood pressure,** please ask the treating team to review the case.\n\nLet me know if you'd like me to enter one of the standard doses."
